{"prompt": "I failed my driving test for the third time and I feel like an idiot.", "response": "Three attempts doesn't make you an idiot — it makes you someone who keeps showing up, which is genuinely hard. Plenty of great drivers needed several tries; the test measures nerves as much as skill. Be gentle with yourself today. When you're ready, ask your examiner's feedback sheet what specifically to practice, and take a lesson focused just on that."}
{"prompt": "My cat died last week and I can't stop feeling guilty that I didn't notice she was sick sooner.", "response": "I'm so sorry. That guilt is a sign of how much you loved her — but cats are famously good at hiding illness; even vets often catch things late. You gave her a home where she felt safe her whole life. Grief takes the time it takes, and it's okay to miss her out loud."}
{"prompt": "I have a big presentation tomorrow and I am so nervous my hands are shaking.", "response": "It is completely normal to feel this way — that nervous energy means you care deeply about doing well. Try some slow, deep breaths: inhale for four counts, hold for four, exhale for six. Remind yourself that you have prepared, and your audience wants you to succeed. You will get through this, one slide at a time."}
{"prompt": "I think I made a terrible mistake at work and my boss is going to fire me.", "response": "I hear how scared you are, and I want to validate that it feels huge right now. Before we spiral, let us ground ourselves: what exactly happened, and is there anything you can clarify or fix today? Most workplaces value honesty and problem-solving. Take a breath, gather your thoughts, and approach your boss with what you learned. You are more capable of handling this than you feel right now."}
{"prompt": "Everyone at my friend group got promoted except me, and I feel like everyone is moving on without me.", "response": "That stings, and it is okay to feel left behind. But your path is your own, not a race against anyone else. Compare yourself only to who you were last month, not to the milestones of others. Would you like to brainstorm some steps for your next review cycle? You deserve growth on your own timeline, and there is no shame in asking for what you need."}
{"prompt": "I just moved to a new city and I feel completely lonely. All my old friends are hours away.", "response": "Moving is one of those life events that looks exciting from the outside but can feel incredibly isolating on the inside. You are not alone in feeling this way. Try reaching out to one local group or class that interests you this week — even small connections can become bridges. And it is perfectly fine to call an old friend today and let them know you miss them."}
